Subject: Recursion depth matches the stack VM's

What this does
  Recursion depth matches the stack VM's.

Why we need it
  `function f{ f; }` overflowed at 192 frames in the monolith and 157 in threaded+record; 4096 B of it a cold `ROP_array_from` `JSValue vals[256]`.

What it adds
  `ROP_array_from` (monolith, `regvm_exec_one`, generated step twin) dups registers straight into the array storage via `regvm_array_from_regs`; the frame arena becomes a chain of never-moving chunks, a new chunk linked when the current one is full, one spare cached, limited by a byte budget of `rt->stack_size` that throws the usual stack-overflow RangeError; `regvm_rec_of_sf` walks the chain.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
